# Vibe Scribe — always-on context

Vibe Scribe is configured for this project. The canonical instructions live in `@AGENTS.md` —
treat that as the always-on behavioral layer and re-load it each turn. (Cursor lacks a literal
"background skill" concept, so this always-applied rule is how the protocol stays active here.)

## Living documents (authoritative project state)

- `@dev-journal.md` — the **log**: append-only history of what changed and *why*. Add a dated entry
  at the end of a chunk of work that made a real system change; never edit past entries.
- `@system-overview.md` — the **map**: current state (component catalog, dependency map, runbook,
  and the **Lexicon** of coined handles). Revise in place; refresh `Last verified` dates.

Keep them distinct: journal = the delta + why; overview = the resulting state. Don't duplicate.
Refer to components by their canonical Lexicon handles.

## Skills

`/briefing` and `/sync` behave identically to their Claude Code / Codex counterparts. Invoke with
`/skill-name` or by describing what you want.

## Cross-vendor compatibility

Ships from a single source for Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, and Cursor. The same `skills/` directory
and the same `AGENTS.md` protocol apply across all three. The only platform-specific files are the
per-host plugin manifests and this Cursor-specific always-on rule.
